      "title": "Mimicking populists will not ease cost of living or boost productivity, Mathias Cormann warns",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/17/mimicking-populists-will-not-ease-cost-of-living-or-raise-productivity-mathias-cormann-warns-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Former minister and OECD head urges Australia not to adopt migration caps, with research showing migrants boost employment among Australian-born workers</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia’s mainstream political parties are being warned not to adopt populist policies such as migration caps to address voters’ grievances over the cost of living.</p><p>Instead, Australia’s longest-serving finance minister Mathias Cormann is urging politicians to deliver housing, real wage growth and lower energy costs by boosting productivity.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/17/mimicking-populists-will-not-ease-cost-of-living-or-raise-productivity-mathias-cormann-warns-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-17T01:49:17"
    },
    {
      "title": "Gone to the dogs: racing fans mourn closure of ‘Wenty’, Sydney’s historic greyhound track",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/17/gone-to-the-dogs-racing-fans-mourn-closure-of-wenty-sydneys-historic-greyhound-track",
      "description": "<p>Thousands pack Wentworth Park for the final time before the stadium is demolished and returned to parkland</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The end of an era has fallen upon an Australian sporting landmark as the greyhound races at an inner-city track kicked off for the very last time.</p><p>Thousands packed into Wentworth Park in central Sydney on Friday night, where greyhound races have been held since 1932, for the last race meeting before the track’s planned demolition.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/17/gone-to-the-dogs-racing-fans-mourn-closure-of-wenty-sydneys-historic-greyhound-track\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-16T23:00:15"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mortgage repayments are now cheaper than rent in some Australian suburbs. Is yours among them?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/17/buying-a-home-cheaper-than-renting-in-some-australian-suburbs",
      "description": "<p>As house prices plateau, the gap between the cost of buying and renting is narrowing in dozens of suburbs</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>High rents and falling property prices have opened a rare window for Australian tenants to become homeowners, with mortgage repayments cheaper than rent in dozens of suburbs.\n <br />\n <br />\n Guardian Australia’s analysis of Cotality data shows that median rents in inner-city Melbourne, suburban Canberra and Darwin are now nearly matching weekly home loan repayments.</p><p>In one in 10 suburbs and towns across the country, repayments are less than $200 a week higher than rent, for the typical property. In some suburbs, they are actually cheaper.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/17/buying-a-home-cheaper-than-renting-in-some-australian-suburbs\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-16T23:00:15"
    }
  ]
